   "evidence": "Lines 279-282 and 296-301; the conclusion `(c.L + 1 = c.J \u2227 c.J + 1 = c'.L \u2228 c'.L + 1 = c.J \u2227 c.J + 1 = c.L)` was introduced by an earlier api-design round (contributor reply 4521648615: \"the mixing theorem now concludes `c.L + 1 = c.J \u2227 c.J + 1 = c'.L \u2228 \u2026`\") without the name following it. Rubric: a name must not advertise an equality the statement does not prove.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Particles/Nuclei/Light/Channel.lean",
   "fix": "Name the symmetric content: introduce a `Prop` for the pair (e.g. `ChannelLabel.IsMixingPair c c' : c.S = 1 \u2227 c'.S = 1 \u2227 (\u2026)`) and rename to `eq_or_isMixingPair` / `eq_or_isMixingPair_of_pauliAllowed`; or, keeping the explicit form, spell both alternatives, e.g. `eq_or_S_eq_one_and_L_add_one_eq_J_or_J_add_one_eq_L`.",
   "issue": "`eq_or_S_eq_one_and_L_add_one_eq_J` reads as `c = c' \u2228 (S = 1 \u2227 c.L + 1 = c.J)`, but the right disjunct is `c.S = 1 \u2227 c'.S = 1 \u2227 (c.L + 1 = c.J \u2227 c.J + 1 = c'.L \u2228 c'.L + 1 = c.J \u2227 c.J + 1 = c.L)`: in the second branch `c.L = c.J + 1`, the opposite of what the name states, and `c'` is absent from the name entirely. Same name, same mismatch at line 296 (`eq_or_S_eq_one_and_L_add_one_eq_J_of_pauliAllowed`), and both are advertised under that name in the module docstring (lines 50-51, 85).",
   "line": "279"
  }
 ],
